      _about: "The book's restraints (ruling 139, the design director's b509(c) and b512(g, h)): at the stops named, a computer staff keeps to what was chosen in the real war even where its own judgement would go further. 'storm': the towns a computer staff, and any computer ally standing round them with it, rings and does not storm (it may still starve them out). 'enter': the ground a computer staff's armies do not go into, to march or to attack. 'fed': a town held by its own side ('nat') whose stores do not run down while the computer staff named ('by') rings it, with no player beside it. 'front' (b527): the seats on that front; where a player holds any one of them none of the restraints applies, so that a player never faces, or fights beside, a city that cannot fall. A player is never held to any of them, and a player's ring starves the town as any other.",
