          _all: "The record gives Japan's boats by command only for the first month, the 63 of December 1941, where America's, Britain's and the Netherlands' rows are dated counts through the war. So the row is marked ('far.all') as the first month's count and no ceiling: every boat the 6th Fleet has goes to the Advance Submarine Fleet the month it is built, and the boats out are the patrol share of what the group has (the design director's ruling of 21:00Z and 21:04Z, 22 November 2026). Before it Japan had 141 boats on hand in August 1945 against the record's 46 or so, and 71 of them lay in the 6th Fleet's harbour all war, where no hunter reached them.",
